patches/engine/independent-sessions.patch adds independent embedded MYSQL handles,
including open/query/close ABI entry points. It raises the InnoDB buffer pool to
64 MiB (maximum resize 256 MiB), the packet limit to 128 MiB, and reserves up to
32 application sessions plus the internal management connection. Closing each
connection lets MariaDB perform its normal rollback and session cleanup.

The patch compiles with PTHREAD_POOL_SIZE=16 and PTHREAD_POOL_SIZE_STRICT=2.
An exhausted worker pool returns EAGAIN instead of creating a worker that cannot
initialize while synchronous native code blocks its creator. Generated browser
logical CPU scheduling is capped at four so InnoDB leaves capacity for background
services. The PHP runtime and native PDO source are unchanged.

Reproduce from the pinned source and Emscripten 6.0.6:
node scripts/build-engine.mjs

The build script, complete patch, source URL, compiler identity and output hashes
are included with the engine. joomengine-patches.json and the release manifest
record the patch, generated glue and rebuilt WASM SHA-256 values. Ship this notice
with the redistributed engine.
